  "live_records": {
    "q-103198": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103198",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $56u+24v=\\text{gcd}(56,24).$ What is the value of $u+v?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}56 & = & 24\\cdot 2 & + & 8 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 24 & = & 8\\cdot 3 & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(56,24)=8.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =56-24\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =56\\cdot 1+24\\cdot (-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $u=1$ and $v=-2.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=1+(-2)=-1.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
