    "q-78471": {
      "dom_id": "step-q78471",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $46u+14v=\\text{gcd}(46,14).$ What is the value of $u+v?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}46 & = & 14\\cdot 3 & + & 4 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 14 & = & 4\\cdot 3 & + & 2 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 4 & = & 2\\cdot 2 & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(14,46)=2.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =46-14\\cdot 3 \\\\ 2 & =14-4\\cdot 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =14-4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =14-[46-14\\cdot 3]\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =14\\cdot 10-46\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =46\\cdot (-3)+14\\cdot 10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=-3$ and $v=10.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=(-3)+10=7.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
