    "q-103211": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103211",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $90u+39v=\\text{gcd}(90,39).$ What is the value of $u+v?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}90 & = & 39\\cdot 2 & + & 12 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 39 & = & 12\\cdot 3 & + & 3 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 12 & = & 3\\cdot 4 & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(90,39)=3.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12 & =90-39\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3 & =39-12\\cdot 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =39-12\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =39-[90-39\\cdot 2]\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =39\\cdot 7-90\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =90\\cdot (-3)+39\\cdot 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=-3$ and $v=7.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=(-3)+7=4.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-103211-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-3",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"44\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-103211-b",
