    "q-78475": {
      "dom_id": "step-q78475",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $72u+30v=\\text{gcd}(72,30).$ What is the value of $u+v?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}72 & = & 30\\cdot 2 & + & 12 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 30 & = & 12\\cdot 2 & + & 6 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 12 & = & 6\\cdot 2 & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(30,72)=6.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12 & =72-30\\cdot 2 \\\\ 6 & =30-12\\cdot 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =30-12\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =30-[72-30\\cdot 2]\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =30\\cdot 5-72\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =72\\cdot (-2)+30\\cdot 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=-2$ and $v=5.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=(-2)+5=3.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
