    "q-79903": {
      "dom_id": "step-q79903",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $53u+24v=\\text{gcd}(53,24).$ What is the value of $u+v?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}53 & = & 24\\cdot 2 & + & 5 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 24 & = & 5\\cdot 4 & + & 4 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 5 & = & 4\\cdot 1 & + & 1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(53,24)=1.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =53-24\\cdot 2 \\\\ 4 & =24-5\\cdot 4 \\\\ 1 & =5-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =5-4 \\\\  & =5-(24-5\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 5-24 \\\\  & =[53-24\\cdot 2]\\cdot 5-24 \\\\  & =53\\cdot 5-24\\cdot 11 \\\\  & =53\\cdot 5+24\\cdot (-11)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=5$ and $v=-11.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=5+(-11)=-6.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
