    "q-77430": {
      "dom_id": "step-q77430",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $47u+20v=\\text{gcd}(47,20).$ What is the value of $u+v?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}47 & = & 20\\cdot 2 & + & 7 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 20 & = & 7\\cdot 2 & + & 6 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 7 & = & 6\\cdot 1 & + & 1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(20,47)=1.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7 & =47-20\\cdot 2 \\\\ 6 & =20-7\\cdot 2 \\\\ 1 & =7-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =7-6 \\\\  & =7-(20-7\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =7\\cdot 3-20 \\\\  & =[47-20\\cdot 2]\\cdot 3-20 \\\\  & =47\\cdot 3-20\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =47\\cdot 3+20\\cdot (-7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=3$ and $v=-7.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=3+(-7)=-4.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
