    "q-103245": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103245",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $49u+20v=\\text{gcd}(49,20).$ What is the value of $u+v?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}49 & = & 20\\cdot 2 & + & 9 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 20 & = & 9\\cdot 2 & + & 2 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 9 & = & 2\\cdot 4 & + & 1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(49,20)=1.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 & =49-20\\cdot 2 \\\\ 2 & =20-9\\cdot 2 \\\\ 1 & =9-2\\cdot 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =9-2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =9-[20-9\\cdot 2]\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =9\\cdot 9-20\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =[49-20\\cdot 2]\\cdot 9-20\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =49\\cdot 9-20\\cdot 22 \\\\  & =49\\cdot 9+20\\cdot (-22)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=9$ and $v=-22.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=9+(-22)=-13.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
