    "q-103244": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103244",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $59u+16v=\\text{gcd}(59,16).$ What is the value of $u+v?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}59 & = & 16\\cdot 3 & + & 11 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 16 & = & 11\\cdot 1 & + & 5 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 11 & = & 5\\cdot 2 & + & 1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(59,16)=1.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11 & =59-16\\cdot 3 \\\\ 5 & =16-11 \\\\ 1 & =11-5\\cdot 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =11-5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =11-(16-11)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =11\\cdot 3-16\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =[59-16\\cdot 3]\\cdot 3-16\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =59\\cdot 3-16\\cdot 11 \\\\  & =59\\cdot 3+16\\cdot (-11)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=3$ and $v=-11.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=3+(-11)=-8.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
